    "top_frame": "This team doesn't need the lead early to win this game.",
    "what_this_means": "Volpe turned a balanced offense into a blowout. The Yankees went ahead in the first inning and never relinquished it, building a 4-run margin by the second before breaking the game open with six runs in the seventh. They scored on five of eighteen RISP plate appearances. Converting opportunities that matter, leaving others alone that didn't. Max Fried lasted just 3.1 innings but the bullpen locked down the finish: Fulmer, Schreiber, Yarbrough, Headrick, and Luis Gil combined for 4.2 scoreless to close it. The shape was wire-to-wire control. Never trailed, never tied after the first. Volpe's five RBI were the separator in a 10-hit game where the lineup did its job and one player made the leverage moments count.",
    "what_to_watch": "The real test is whether this holds. They are three games into a streak while sitting three back in the division. Volpe delivered when the game was already in hand. Offense-heavy wins like this can feel fragile if the next game asks the defense or pitching to carry a tighter result. They had runway and used it. The question now is what happens when the margin shrinks. Three straight wins is building something. Three straight one-run wins would be unsustainable.",
